claimed: intent-end-to-end — nothing calls any of this. Thirteen files and twenty measured lanes, and inside okay there is no path where a message arrives and a decision leaves; a consumer has their own router, okay-intent has no caller of its own. Build the caller: a demo that classifies a real message with the tiers as shipped, composes them the way the spec argues for, fills a Frame and asks what is missing. The point is NOT another number. A library with no callers has the wrong API and cannot know it, and there is already one symptom -- Frame.filled throws away the parsed value, which surfaced the moment I wrote how it would be used and never in a test. Expect to find more, and record what the exercise breaks rather than quietly fixing it.
